  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mississippi has $6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 85,905 awards, with an average award size of $69.7K, and obligations fell 25.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $5B so far. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations at $3.7B. Top vendors reflect that concentration: HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED received $3.6B, dwarfing other vendors such as V2X AEROSPACE LLC at $466M and NOVA SPACE SOLUTIONS, LLC at $109M. Other notable agency buys include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $350M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $161M. Facilities Support Services, Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction, and Industrial Building Construction also appear among the top industries, with respective obligations of $169M, $155M, and $115M. These figures are partial because FY2026 is still in progress, and they represent contract obligations recorded through the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the current FY2026 total?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5B, which accounts for the majority of the $6B total. Ship Building and Repairing accounted for $3.7B of obligations, concentrating spending in one industry. Obligations fell 25.2% year over year, so the current total reflects both large DoD and shipbuilding awards and an overall downshift versus the prior year. FY2026 totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate Mississippi federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer at $5B, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $350M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $161M. Ship Building and Repairing leads industries with $3.7B, followed by Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $507M and Facilities Support Services at $169M. HUNTINGTON INGALLS INCORPORATED is the largest vendor at $3.6B, with V2X AEROSPACE LLC at $466M and NOVA SPACE SOLUTIONS, LLC at $109M rounding out the top vendors."
      }
    ]
  },
